 "label": "Bulge Through",
 "category": "Transition",
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "The lens warp transition: the picture swells out into a fisheye bubble round a point, with colour fringes at its edge, and pushes in until the cut; the next clip settles back out of the same bubble. Put it on both clips of a cut, or use Progress to key it by hand. The picture repeats round the edges, so no gap shows.",
